rust-proxmox-product-config (1.1.0-1) trixie; urgency=medium

  * add a ProductConfig type holding the API and privileged users and the
    configuration, state, runtime and cache directories, and providing the
    matching file and directory creation options. Applications can keep it in
    their own context instead of relying on global state, which also allows
    tests to use temporary directories and the current user.

  * update to edition 2024.

  * documentation: correct the stated owners and permissions of the file and
    lock file helpers. For example, replace_config() creates files with mode
    0640, not 0660, and files of the privileged helpers are owned by the
    configured privileged user, which is not necessarily root.

 -- Proxmox Support Team <support@proxmox.com>  Mon, 12 Oct 2026 18:35:33 +0200

